CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "99fd3d04-aaa0-410b-bf82-e80bff09976c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-22T01:33:01Z",
  "ticket_id": "d566-afa6-1aa3-4293",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "SC1: plugins/dso/skills/shared/prompts/behavioral-testing-standard.md gains Rule 6 \u2014 every NEW or MODIFIED test in the diff carries a fenced \"## Test Intent\" header above the test function with fields intent_id (SC|DoD|AC reference from parent ticket subtree, or \"UNTRACKED \u2014 <one-line rationale>\" permitted sentinel) and catches_regression_where (sentence-completion form: \"this test turns RED if and only if [specific production-code change]\"). Rule 6 includes canonical per-language header fixture examples covering Python (docstring with markdown fence inside), JavaScript/TypeScript (block comment with markdown fence inside), and bash (line-comment block with markdown fence inside). Legacy tests not modified in the diff are exempt.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable rule and documentation standard that governs test structure going forward, phrased as an ongoing property of the file and testing practice"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC2: behavioral-testing-standard.md gains Rule 7 \u2014 when adding behavioral coverage for an intent_id already claimed by an existing test, add a sibling parameterized case or new sibling test function in the same test file. Do NOT append assertions to an existing test function. Do NOT create a duplicate test function claiming the same intent_id without an orthogonal scenario suffix. Each test function carries at most one \"## Test Intent\" header. behavioral-testing-standard.md is designated a safeguard file per CLAUDE.md rule 22 \u2014 sub-agents may not propose edits that weaken Rule 6 or 7 without explicit user approval.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable rule and enforcement mechanism that, once established in the standard document, remains an ongoing system property governing test structure"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC3: Three test-writing surfaces updated to reference Rules 6 and 7 in their generation guidance: plugins/dso/agents/red-test-writer.md, plugins/dso/skills/sprint/prompts/task-execution.md, and the fix-bug RED-phase prompt (concrete path under plugins/dso/skills/fix-bug/ resolved during implementation-plan). Synthetic verification: a dispatch of dso:red-test-writer against a fixture task containing one AC produces a test file whose header parses under the per-language syntax appendix and whose intent_id field exactly matches the fixture AC identifier; parse success is confirmed by an automated grep that finds the fenced \"## Test Intent\" block, the intent_id field, and the catches_regression_where field in the output.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability (test-writing surfaces correctly reference Rules 6 and 7 with verifiable output properties) that remains true after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC4: plugins/dso/docs/workflows/prompts/reviewer-delta-test-quality.md (the build source for the compiled plugins/dso/agents/code-reviewer-test-quality.md agent, regenerated via build-review-agents.sh) gains two new review dimensions. Tier 1 (assertion shape) emits a finding when a test assertion targets internal method names, private state, mock-invocation counts (e.g., mock.called_with), or source-grep patterns against source files; requires assertions to target observable outputs (return values, exit codes, file contents, side effects, emitted events). Tier 2 (articulation) emits a finding when (a) a new/modified test has missing or malformed header, (b) catches_regression_where is tautological, (c) the assertions do not exercise the intent named in intent_id (REQUIRED scaffold: reviewer first lists the observable artifact each assert measures, then lists what intent_id claims is measured, then flags if these two sets are disjoint), (d) catches_regression_where would not in fact cause the test to fail given the assertions present, (e) duplicate intent_id without orthogonal scenario suffix or sibling-case structure per Rule 7. Dimension carries an anti-sycophancy prime: \"Identify the single most damaging flaw. If no flaw exists, state 'No findings' explicitly.\" The build pipeline regenerates code-reviewer-test-quality.md from this delta source as part of the implementation work.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable reviewer agent capabilities (two new review dimensions with specific detection rules) that will exist in the system after implementation, phrased as behavioral properties the agent will exhibit"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC5: A /dso:review run against a synthetic diff containing (a) a new test with no header, (b) a new test asserting only on mock.called_with(...), (c) a new test whose intent_id claims SC-1 but whose only assertion is `assert True == True`, produces a reviewer-findings.json where the findings[] array includes at least one entry with dimension matching \"Tier 1 (assertion shape)\" or \"Tier 2 (articulation)\" AND whose source_path:source_line falls inside violations (a), (b), (c) respectively. The same findings[] array contains zero entries with those dimensions whose source_line falls inside any unmodified legacy test block in the same diff.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability to detect and report specific test quality violations with precise dimension categorization in its output"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC6: Pointer/version updates for the consumer files explicitly known to reference the behavioral testing standard or its Rule 5 ordinal:\n- plugins/dso/skills/implementation-plan/SKILL.md\n- plugins/dso/skills/implementation-plan/docs/reviewers/plan/tdd.md\n- plugins/dso/skills/preplanning/SKILL.md\n- plugins/dso/docs/workflows/prompts/review-fix-dispatch.md\n- plugins/dso/agents/red-test-evaluator.md (plus: rejection criteria extended to require Rule 6 header on new test output)\n- plugins/dso/skills/fix-bug/SKILL.md (the \"Apply all five rules\" enumeration)\n- plugins/dso/docs/AGENTS.md (the \"detects 5 test bloat patterns\" count)\n- tests/hooks/test-behavioral-testing-standard-rule5.sh (preamble-count assertion made version-agnostic, or removed in favor of the existing test_rule_count_matches_headings assertion which uses -ge 5)\n- tests/scripts/test-red-test-writer-md-rule5-compliance.sh (heading assertion made version-agnostic or extended)\n- tests/hooks/test-agent-standard-reference.sh (heading assertion made version-agnostic or extended)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes one-time updates to pointers and version references across multiple files, which is a discrete migration task rather than an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC7 (dogfood): The tests written for d566's own implementation carry valid Rule 6 headers. A /dso:review run on the d566 implementation PR emits zero Tier 1 or Tier 2 findings on those tests.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the system state (tests carry valid headers and review runs produce zero findings) that persists after the work, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC8 (explicit descope): plugins/dso/hooks/pre-commit-test-quality-gate.sh and plugins/dso/hooks/semgrep-rules/test-anti-patterns.yaml are explicitly NOT extended by this epic. Rule 6 + Rule 7 enforcement is review-only via the dimensions added to code-reviewer-test-quality in SC4. If future evidence supports adding hook-level enforcement, a follow-on epic will scope it.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable scope boundary of the system\u2014these specific files are excluded from enforcement in this epic, establishing an ongoing property of what the system does and does not enforce"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC9 (structural sweep): During implementation, the implementer runs the following case-insensitive grep across plugins/, tests/, and docs/ (file types: *.md, *.sh, *.py, *.yaml, *.yml):",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time sweep task to be executed during implementation, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
